<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umur Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1309–<a href="/years/1348">1348</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umur Bey was ruler of the Aydinid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from 1334. From Smyrna his fleets raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> islands and Greek coasts, and he allied with the Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a>. His raids provoked the Smyrniote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>, which took Smyrna harbour in 1344; he was killed attempting to retake it in 1348.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/umur-bey.jpg" alt="Umur Bey" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kusadasi500 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umur_beyaydin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
